Heap card (text):

HPK1
NODE <id> <class> <bytes>
EDGE <from> <to> KIND <field>
ROOT <id> <rootKind>
SITE <id>
END

KIND is STRONG or WEAK.
A retaining chain uses STRONG edges only.
PATH is hop labels of a shortest retaining chain from a ROOT to the SITE.
When several STRONG hops reach SITE, PATH uses the class.field of the STRONG hop into SITE.

Ledger lines, SITE class ascending:

SITE <class>
BYTES <n>
PATH <rootKind>><Class>.<field>>...><Class>.<field>

align writes /app/inkurn/align.txt
  lock
or
  slip
--- BAY.txt ---
Pipeline modules:

- /app/rootwell
- /app/adjmill
- /app/softbay

CLI lives under /app/millarm. Rebuild with /app/kindle.sh. Desk also links with make -C /app/millarm -f driver.mk OUT=/tmp/keelgrip.ref.

`--pin-handles` reorders neighbour lists by object id. Ops turned it on when PATH drifted; SITE and BYTES still matched.
